# Environment Variables

## Access

**Core app config** — `~/shared/lib/env`:

```typescript
import { env } from "~/shared/lib/env";

env.WORKSPACE_API_ORIGIN // optional default origin (multi-org uses instance at runtime)
env.WORKSPACE_API_BASE // dev: `/workspace{rest}`; prod: origin + rest or override
env.JITSI_MEET_DOMAIN
env.JITSI_MEET_BASE_URL
env.WORKSPACE_UPLOADS_ORIGIN
env.ZULIP_API_PATH
env.WORKSPACE_API_PATH
env.CDN_URL
env.BASE_URL
env.DEV
env.PROD
```

**Integrations** (read `import.meta.env` in dedicated modules — do not duplicate in `env.ts` unless widely used): `~/shared/lib/brand` (`VITE_BRAND_*`), analytics (`VITE_GA4_*`, `VITE_YM_*`), FCM (`VITE_FIREBASE_*`), `VITE_APP_VERSION` in UI, `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` in `sentry.ts`.

## Rules

- Prefer `env` or a single module (`brand`, `analytics/setup`) per concern — avoid scattering new `import.meta.env` reads in random components.
- `constants.ts` re-exports from `env` for backward compatibility.
- New **core** env vars: add to `ImportMetaEnv` in `vite-env.d.ts`, parsing in `shared/lib/env.ts` if part of the core object, and `.env.example`.

## Variables (core `env`)

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `VITE_WORKSPACE_API_ORIGIN` | No | Optional default API/realm host; multi-org uses instance + `X-Workspace-Dev-Target-Origin` in dev |
| `VITE_WORKSPACE_API_PATH` / `VITE_WORKSPACE_REST_API_PATH` / `VITE_USER_UPLOADS_PATH_PREFIX` / `VITE_ZULIP_API_PATH` | No | When unset, defaults come from `~/shared/config/workspace-api-layout` (gateway-first; vanilla: set `/api/v1` — ADR-008) |
| `VITE_JITSI_MEET_DOMAIN` | No | Jitsi Meet domain (without protocol) |
| `VITE_WORKSPACE_API_BASE_URL` | No | Override Workspace REST base |
| `VITE_ZULIP_API_PATH` | No | Zulip API path (default `/api/v1`) |
| `VITE_WORKSPACE_API_PATH` | No | Workspace API path (default `/api/v1`) |
| `VITE_CDN_URL` | No | CDN origin for static assets |
| `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` | No | Sentry DSN (production only when set; see `sentry.ts`) |
| `VITE_APP_VERSION` | No | Version string for Sentry / about UI |
| `ELECTRON` | No | Build-time (Vite config): disables PWA, `./` base — set by Electron `npm` scripts, not usually in `.env` |

See `vite-env.d.ts` for the full `VITE_*` list (flags, embed, metadata bootstrap, brand, etc.).

## Security

- `VITE_*` variables end up in the client bundle — DO NOT store secrets
- API Key is stored in localStorage, not in env vars
- `ELECTRON` does NOT have the `VITE_` prefix — not exposed to client bundle via Vite env injection

## Environment files (Vite order)

```
.env                 ← always loaded
.env.local           ← always, gitignored
.env.development     ← only npm run dev
.env.production      ← only npm run build
.env.[mode].local    ← mode-specific, gitignored
```
